{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788114143,"nonce":"tRSxHAI8NEyRqTitaYE5i1Qk100=","message":"Open-question resolution 1/3 — profile script layout, flags, bench path (worker, spike 0.1).\n\nBench path: /home/dorian/projects/rimworld/_RimWorld-Agent — workspace sibling of _RimWorld-Test/_RimWorld-Testing, exactly as the pre-flight note proposed. make-profile-agent.sh derives it as $RIMWORLD_VAULT/_RimWorld-Agent (RIMWORLD_VAULT defaulting to /home/dorian/projects/rimworld) so the _meta convention holds.\n\nLayout: the repo's profile/ dir is the source of truth and holds three committed files — make-profile-agent.sh (builds the farm), gen-modsconfig.py (copied from _RimWorld-Test per spec instruction, adapted HEAD/TAIL), run-agent.sh (launcher). make-profile-agent.sh COPIES the latter two into the built profile rather than symlinking them there: run-agent.sh self-locates via readlink -f, which through a symlink would resolve into the repo and defeat both its path guard and gen-modsconfig's Mods/ discovery. The profile itself is a disposable build artifact; re-running make-profile-agent.sh is idempotent and refreshes the copies.\n\nrun-agent.sh flags: --fps N (mangohud cap, default 30, live-editable via MANGOHUD_CONFIGFILE while running), --quicktest, --xvfb (+--vnc), --batchmode, --no-rule, --no-modsconfig; everything else passes through to RimWorldLinux. Guard: refuses to run unless its dir is */_RimWorld-Agent — this launcher cannot start any other install.\n\nTwo non-obvious behaviors that are now part of the layout contract, both learned from failed boots (full story in FINDINGS.md §1):\n(1) the RimWorldLinux stub is a REAL COPY, not a symlink — /proc/self/exe canonicalizes symlinks and re-roots the game at the Steam install, silently swapping in Steam's Mods/;\n(2) run-agent.sh regenerates ModsConfig.xml on every launch, because RimWorld rewrites that file whenever it prunes mods it cannot resolve, and the pruned list otherwise persists into every later launch.","files":null}]}